From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:25:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 342/353] drm/apple: iomfb_m4: send the internal panel's flip
 with its swap's completion

The internal panel's present waited inside the atomic commit for the
swap's own completion (D590), 3.3 ms after the firmware accepted it
(A407) on average, most of it the wait for the panel's next tick, and
the flip event then said refresh 0 and the time the commit returned:
the driver never calls drm_vblank_init().

The commit now returns once the firmware has accepted the swap. The
swap waits in one slot (r->int_fl, the external path's hand-off at
depth 1) until its D590, which puts its frame on screen and sends the
flip event, stamped with the time the D590 arrived (taken in the
mailbox receive path for every word) and with the panel's refresh
count: the last one plus the refreshes since the previous flip at the
running rate.

The flip still comes no earlier than the D590. DRM hands the previous
framebuffer back to the compositor with it, and that framebuffer is
scanned out until the D590: it stays dcp->active_fb, referenced, until
the D590 promotes the new frame, and only then is the event sent. A
D590 that says the frame was not displayed keeps every frame that may
still be on screen (lost_fb, extra_fb) until a displayed one retires
them.

At most one internal swap is open: every host call of our own (the
next swap's A406, a blank, a power state, a mode set, an idle-cache or
power-gate call) first waits for the open swap's D590, as the commit
did before. A D590 that does not come within 5 s fails the session as
it did, with the flip sent as lost. Framebuffers retired by a D590 are
put by a work item, outside the lock. The idle worker that handles a
D590 nobody waits for runs at high priority on the internal DCP.

XDR probe swaps keep the synchronous path (their given-up rule needs
the D590 in the commit), as do blanks and brightness-only swaps.
swap_pace is unchanged; its base is now the D590's arrival.

The m4tl present timeline gains ret_cnt (when the present returned),
appended to each line; flip_cnt / flip_ns are when the flip was sent.

int_async_flip=N restores the synchronous path from the next frame.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
